# Example calls for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or any .http runner that supports named requests).
# Start the stack first: see the README. The operator is the one set in .env (OPERATOR_EMAIL / OPERATOR_PASSWORD).

@host = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Register two customers
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1"}

###
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ben@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1"}

### 2. Log in (each login names its response so later calls can reuse the token)
# @name loginAna
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1"}

###
# @name loginBen
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ben@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1"}

###
# @name loginOperator
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "operator@bank.test", "password": "change-me-operator-password"}

###
@ana = {{loginAna.response.body.token}}
@ben = {{loginBen.response.body.token}}
@operator = {{loginOperator.response.body.token}}

### 3. Each customer opens an account (ids are 1 and 2 on a fresh database)
POST {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

###
POST {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{ben}}

### 4. The operator funds ana's account: 50,000 centavos = 500.00 MXN
POST {{host}}/accounts/1/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": 50000}

### 5. Ana transfers 12,345 centavos to ben. The Idempotency-Key makes retries safe.
POST {{host}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"sourceAccountId": 1, "targetAccountId": 2, "amount": 12345}

### 6. Send the exact same request again: same response, and the money moves only once
POST {{host}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"sourceAccountId": 1, "targetAccountId": 2, "amount": 12345}

### 7. Same key, different amount: 422
POST {{host}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"sourceAccountId": 1, "targetAccountId": 2, "amount": 99999}

### 8. History of ana's account, newest first
GET {{host}}/accounts/1/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### 9. Ben cannot see ana's account: 404, not 403
GET {{host}}/accounts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{ben}}

### 10. The operator freezes ana's account; a new transfer from it is a 409
POST {{host}}/accounts/1/freeze
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### 11. The operator reads the audit log, filtered by action
GET {{host}}/audit?action=TRANSFER
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
